708
00:55:13,980 --> 00:55:14,020
Okay?

709
00:55:16,420 --> 00:55:20,690
The basic idea here
is that if I take

710
00:55:22,310 --> 00:55:25,780
the k -th vertex in
the topological order,

711
00:55:26,820 --> 00:55:29,840
assuming that these
distances are all equal

712
00:55:30,520 --> 00:55:32,700
for the ones before me
in the topological order,

713
00:55:33,220 --> 00:55:34,980
I can prove by induction. Right?

714
00:55:36,380 --> 00:55:38,110
So I can take the
shortest path from s to v.

715
00:55:38,900 --> 00:55:39,950
Right? The k -th vertex.

716
00:55:41,740 --> 00:55:46,280
And look at the vertex preceding me
along the shortest path. Right? That

717
00:55:47,300 --> 00:55:47,980
vertex better

718
00:55:49,500 --> 00:55:53,320
be before me in the topological
order, or we're not a DAG.

719
00:55:53,840 --> 00:55:54,060
Right?

720
00:55:54,560 --> 00:55:57,280
And we've already set its
shortest path distance to be equal

721
00:55:58,260 --> 00:56:00,720
to the correct
thing by induction.

722
00:56:03,080 --> 00:56:05,800
So then when we
processed u, right?

723
00:56:08,320 --> 00:56:11,680
S to u to v.

724
00:56:12,520 --> 00:56:17,120
When we processed u
in DAG relaxation here,

725
00:56:17,640 --> 00:56:20,720
processed the vertex and looked
at all its outgoing adjacencies,

726
00:56:21,580 --> 00:56:27,860
we would have relaxed this edge to be no
greater than that shortest path distance.

727
00:56:32,340 --> 00:56:33,480
So this is correct. But

728
00:56:35,020 --> 00:56:36,060
you can also think of it

729
00:56:36,820 --> 00:56:44,180
as the DAG relaxation algorithm for each
vertex looks all at its incoming neighbors,

730
00:56:45,460 --> 00:56:49,000
assuming that their shortest path
distances are computed correctly already.

731
00:56:49,820 --> 00:56:55,050
Right? Any shortest path distance to me needs to be composed
of a shortest path distance to one of my incoming neighbors

732
00:56:55,740 --> 00:56:57,160
through an edge to me.

733
00:56:58,940 --> 00:57:00,280
So I can just check all of them.

734
00:57:00,880 --> 00:57:02,900
That's what DAG
relaxation kind of does.

735
00:57:03,920 --> 00:57:04,380
And again,

736
00:57:04,900 --> 00:57:08,460
we're looping over every vertex and looking
at its adjacencies, doing constant work.

737
00:57:09,100 --> 00:57:10,900
This again takes linear time.

738
00:57:11,460 --> 00:57:14,120
OK. So that's shortest
paths in a DAG.

739
00:57:16,100 --> 00:57:21,570
Next time, we'll look at, for general graphs,
how we can use kind of the same technique

740
00:57:22,920 --> 00:57:25,120
in an algorithm we
call Bellman -Ford. OK.

741
00:57:25,680 --> 00:57:26,420
That's it for today.

